The function uses a generator expression to iterate over the first `k` elements of `arr`. The generator expression `(elem for elem in arr[:k])` generates each element of the first `k` elements of `arr`.

The `if len(str(elem)) <= 2` part is a condition that filters out the elements of `arr` that have more than two digits. The `len(str(elem))` part converts the element to a string and counts the number of digits in the string. If the number of digits is 2 or less, the element is included in the sum.

